          "Adult diagnostic reasoning commonly combines ovulatory features, androgen-related findings and ovarian markers while excluding other explanations. In clinic, the practical question is what this changes: whether observation is enough, whether examination or a selected test could add information, and which professional should lead care. Dr. Charmi Shah should explain the limits of the assessment as clearly as its findings. Routine booking remains separate from urgent local care for severe or rapidly worsening symptoms.",
