          "Bring vaccination records, previous scan or operation reports, cervical-screening information and important blood-test results if available. Ask which vaccinations or tests are appropriate for you and when they should occur. A universal online test panel often creates expense without answering an individual clinical question.",
          "Chronic conditions should be reviewed for stability and pregnancy implications without suggesting that someone must achieve perfect health before conceiving. This matters because two people asking “What should I do before trying for a baby?” may need different next steps even when one surface detail sounds similar. A review should establish what began first, what has changed, which treatments or adaptations have already been tried, and what would count as meaningful improvement. That is more clinically useful than promising one standard programme or deadline.",
